  "body": "### Summary\nroger21 publishes the server code of the AQ service (`roger21/toyo`, folder `aq/`) and the reference userscript (`roger21/hfr`). Both are under AGPL-3.0. They give the full `addAlerte.php` contract, which matches our capture T50/T51 (#531). Record the facts, fix our stale docs, and set a policy for third-party sources. Requested by the operator, 2026-11-07.\n\n### Sources (read-only, 2026-11-07)\n- `roger21/toyo@96c0aeafdbfc6dfdd63746a6be65a79f227c5860`: `aq/api/addAlerte.php`, `aq/api/getAlertesByTopic.php`, `aq/rss.php`, `aq/config/alerteQualitay.config.php`, `aq/dao/*`, `aq/sql/db.sql`. Use only the schema of `db.sql`, at lines 31-37 and 1564-1577. **The file is a real dump with real pseudos: never copy it.**\n- `roger21/hfr@b8d110b10fae3096bc547fc0cbc06be1266d18a9`: `hfr_alerte_quali_mod_r21.user.js`, lines 799-861 and 1012-1120.\n- The HFR topic \"Pimp my HFR • Scripts & Extensions\" (`sujet_148758`).\n\n### Contract summary\n- Create: `POST /api/addAlerte.php`, form-urlencoded, UTF-8. Answer body: `1` OK, `-1` insert failed, `-2` unknown AQ, `-3` missing parameter, `-4` duplicate.\n- **Silent refusals:**\n  - 403 with an empty body when the IP is blacklisted or `post_url` does not start with `https://forum.hardware.fr`;\n  - 200 with an empty body for the 60 s anti-flood (3 or more new AQs from one IP). The server then **deletes those AQs and bans the IP**.\n  - So the app sends one create at a time and never retries.\n- Duplicate keys: (`alerte_qualitay_id`, `pseudo`) and (`pseudo`, `post_url`), case-insensitive. The app must always send one stable permalink form.\n- Adding to an existing AQ: `alerte_qualitay_id=<id>`.\n- Limits: `nom`, `topic_titre`, `post_url` ≤512; `pseudo` ≤128; `commentaire` ≤1024.\n- Optional `from` client identifier.\n- RSS parameters: `entries`, `minimal_votes`, `enable_smilies`.\n- The server stores a hashed IP under a published key (reversible for IPv4) and e-mails its operator on each create. Mention this in the LOT-071 / N1 notice.\n\n### To do (one PR, docs only)\n1. HFR-PROTOCOL §8, the `aq.super-h.fr` row:\n   - \"create verified (T50, T51)\";\n   - a \"Server source (secondary, not a capture)\" paragraph citing `repo@SHA:file:line`;\n   - every refusal marked *pending capture (local instance)*.\n2. Fix the stale claims:\n   - `docs/lots/LOT-055-aq-client.md:62` and `LOT-071-third-party-services.md:29, 53`: legacy did **not** lose accents, because it percent-encodes before the ASCII conversion (`MessagesView.swift:389-396, 434-437` @ 2440d79);\n   - the `AQAlert.swift:1` comment (\"unverified\").\n3. **ADR 0015, \"Third-party open-source code as a protocol source\":**\n   - a secondary source, cited `repo@SHA:file:line`;\n   - facts only, never code (AGPL vs PolyForm-NC);\n   - captures stay the oracle;\n   - states known only from the source are handled on the safe side;\n   - refusal states may be captured from a local instance at a pinned SHA;\n   - running a third-party server in CI needs its own ADR.\n\n### Open decision for LOT-134 (#224)\nLegacy stops if **anyone** already reported the post. The server only refuses the same pseudo, and accepts adding to an existing AQ (\"plussoiement\"). The operator decides whether to follow the server or legacy.\n\n### Routing\nThe docs part is written by Haiku 5.5 and reviewed by Opus 5.5. The ADR is written by Opus 5.5 and reviewed by Fable 5.1. The ADR is merged by the core orchestrator or the maintainer (AGENTS.md §8).\n\n### Related\n- #81 (LOT-055), #224 (LOT-134), #223 (LOT-133), #531.\n- The local-instance capture issue.\n- Contacting roger21 is a public action: it waits for the operator (AGENTS.md §0).",
