   "body": "**roger21's answer** (author of the AQ service), private message to the operator, 2026-11-07. Technical facts only:\n\n1. **Source = prod.** The `aq/` code on `roger21/toyo` is exactly what runs in production, connection settings aside (documented in `aq/` at the repo root). The `random` branch only differs in the generators; the AQ code is identical on both branches. → `roger21/toyo@96c0aea` is a faithful secondary source for the `addAlerte.php` contract (ADR 0015 still applies: facts only, captures remain the oracle).\n2. **`from` field.** It exists to identify the client. It is not stored in the database, only in the server logs and the notification e-mail. Free value. **Decided (operator):** SwiftHFR sends `from=SwiftHFR`.\n3. **Testing.** A local instance runs on any PHP 8 + MySQL/MariaDB. Testing on the production server is also accepted: put \"test\" in the AQ and/or the message, and roger21 can delete the test AQs.\n   - **Decided (operator):** the Mac captures the success cases **on production**, marked \"test\", one request at a time and at most one per minute: new AQ, plussoiement, and attaching a post to an existing AQ.\n   - Refusal cases that trigger the anti-flood or the blacklist stay on a **local instance** (#574), because they ban the IP.\n4. **Load.** No constraint is wanted for now. RSS and `getAlertesByTopic` are already polled on every topic page by every HFR+ user without trouble. `entries` / `minimal_votes` values (5 vs 50) make no real difference. Only fetching every AQ each time would be a problem. The anti-flood only handles extreme cases (about 3 AQs in under a minute from one IP; the exact rule is in `addAlerte.php`).\n5. **Scope.** The third use case, attaching another post to an existing AQ, is optional. Plussoiement is wanted. This is consistent with the decision recorded on #224.\n\nTo do from this:\n- **HFR-PROTOCOL §8:** record points 1, 2 and 4 in the docs PR of this issue.\n- **LOT-055 (#81):** send `from=SwiftHFR`.\n- **#574:** scope split as above (comment there).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
